<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
    What the hardened runtime lets the program do beyond its defaults: one thing.

    Apple events: File Properties asks Finder for the Get Info window (through osascript), and
    the commands the user starts may control other applications. The system still asks the
    user once per application (NSAppleEventsUsageDescription in Info.plist).

    Deliberately absent, so the runtime keeps refusing them:
    - com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables: DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES and
      DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH stay without effect on the program.
    - com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation: only libraries of the system and of
      the program's own signature are loaded (the one library opened by name,
      /usr/lib/libicucore.A.dylib, is the system's).
    - com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory,
      disable-executable-page-protection: the program generates no code.
    - com.apple.security.get-task-allow: no debugger attaches to a built program.
    The App Sandbox is not used: a file manager works on every folder the user can reach.
-->
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
